-
-## Findings
-
-| ID | Severity | File/line | Issue | Recommended fix | Expected verification |
-|---|---|---|---|---|---|
-| DSI-DOM-01 | High | `standards/architecture/02-shared-kernel.md:27`, `standards/architecture/02-shared-kernel.md:39`, `packages/shared/domain/src/entity/EntityId.ts:388`, `packages/shared/domain/src/entity/EntityMixin.ts:67`, `packages/shared/domain/src/entity/primitives.ts:2` | The shared-domain package now owns generic identity/modeling/storage primitives (`EntityId.factory`, `EntityMixin`, generic crypto/clock primitives). The shared-kernel standard explicitly excludes generic schema kits, identity kits, reusable technical capability packages, and product-agnostic substrate from shared. `BaseEntity`, `Principal`, shared IDs, and `Organization` are product-language candidates; the generic constructor kit underneath them needs a boundary decision. | Move generic identity/mixin/primitives to the foundation/modeling layer and keep shared-domain exports as shared product vocabulary, or amend the architecture docs with an explicit rationale that this entity kernel is shared-kernel language rather than foundation substrate. | Imports updated without product/driver leakage; `bun run check`, `bun run test`, targeted TSTyche, lint, and docgen pass after the boundary decision. |
-| DSI-DOM-02 | High | `packages/shared/domain/src/entity/BaseEntity.ts:416`, `packages/shared/domain/src/entity/BaseEntity.ts:424`, `packages/shared/domain/src/entity/BaseEntity.ts:439`, `packages/shared/tables/src/table/Table.ts:323` | `BaseEntity.extend` accepts entity-specific fields and places them on the model, but `definition.fieldMap` is built only from id, base fields, and mixins. A runtime probe showed a direct `title` field appears in `Doc.fields` but not in `Doc.definition.fieldMap`; table derivation also consumes `BaseEntity.fieldMapFor(entityId, mixins)`, so persisted direct fields cannot get table metadata. | Either add descriptor input for entity-specific fields and merge it into `definition.fieldMap`, or make direct entity-specific persisted fields unsupported by type/API and require persisted fields to be supplied through `EntityMixin`. | Runtime and TSTyche tests assert `Document.definition.fieldMap.title` and derived table columns when direct fields are supported, or assert compile/runtime rejection when they are not. |
-| DSI-DOM-03 | Medium | `packages/shared/domain/src/entities/Organization/Organization.values.ts:99`, `packages/shared/domain/src/entities/Organization/Organization.values.ts:128` | `parentOrgId` is documented/described as nullable storage (`nullable: true`) but modeled with `S.OptionFromOptionalKey(Shared.OrganizationId)`. It decodes omission to `O.none()`, but rejects `null` with `Expected SharedOrganizationId, got null`. That is a mismatch for a nullable boundary. | Use the repo's nullish Option boundary (`S.OptionFromNullishOr` or the nearest current equivalent) if database/API nulls are valid, or set the descriptor to non-nullable and document omission-only semantics. | Add runtime tests for omitted, `null`, valid id, and invalid id inputs; add TSTyche assertions that the runtime type remains `O.Option<Shared.OrganizationId>`. |
